# Docker reads this file, not .gitignore, when assembling the build context.
#
# Without it `COPY . .` drops the host's node_modules on top of the one `npm ci`
# just built. On a Windows workstation that tree carries win32 binaries
# (@esbuild/win32-x64, @rollup/rollup-win32-x64-msvc) and .cmd/.ps1 shims, and
# because docker-compose.yml seeds the anonymous /app/node_modules volume from
# this image, they end up running inside the Linux container. It is also ~200 MB
# of context that invalidates the cache on every source edit.
node_modules
dist
.vite

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
